{
 "regions": {
  "r2": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "mind for a moment; there are many clouds in the sky, but",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "they are not all of them such ( that a supplication should",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "be addressed to them ); some of them moisten the earth",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "with showers, ( whereas ) others roar for nothing; do not",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "utter a piteous cry before every one that you happen to see.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r3": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "52. Cruelty, unprovoked opposition, lust of another’s",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "wealth and wife, and envy of good men and relations: these",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "are natural with the wicked.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r4": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "53. Though adorned with learning a wicked man should",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "be avoided. Is not a serpent dangerous ( although it is ) be-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "decked with a jewel ?",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r5": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "54. Dulness is attributed to a modest man; hypocrisy to",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "one who has a liking for religious observences; roguery to",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "one who leads a life of sanctity; cruelty to a warrior; want",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "of discrimination to one devoted to meditation; meanness to",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "one who speaks agreeably; arrogance to a spirited man; gar-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "rulity to an orator; and imbecility to a steady man. What",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "virtue is there then that is not stigmatised by the wicked ?",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r6": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "55. If avarice forms part of a man’s character, why",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "should he need other bad qualities; if there be wickedness,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "why want sins; if truthfulness, religious austerietis; if there",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "is purity of heart, why should he go on a pilgrimage ? If he",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "has goodness of heart, why should he want relatives ? If he",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "has reputation, ornaments are superfluous. If he possesses",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "learning, what need he care for wealth ( v. l. the people )?",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "If he has a bad name why should he need death ?",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r7": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "56. The moon, pale by day ( i. e. day-light ), a beautiful",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "woman past youth, a lake without lotuses, the unlettered",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "mouth of a man with a fair exterior, a king solely given to",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "hoarding wealth, a virtuous man ever plunged in misery,",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r1": {
   "type": "page_number",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "[ 10 ]",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  }
 },
